9 — RAG & Suggested Replies (vector DB + LLM)
Workflow:
1. Store product/outreach agenda docs in Weaviate (or Milvus). 
Each item has text + metadata + embedding vector.
2. For any Interested email, compute embedding of email body, 
query the vector DB for top-k related product/agenda docs.
3. Build prompt: include retrieved docs + email content + 
instruction to suggest 2 short replies (tone: polite, reply options: 
short and long, include CTA).
4. Call LLM with the prompt; save suggested replies to 
Elasticsearch under suggestedReplies.
Example pseudocode for RAG:
import weaviate from "weaviate-ts-client";
import axios from "axios";
const client = weaviate.client({ scheme: "http", host: 
"localhost:8080" });
async function suggestReplies(emailDoc) {

// 1. get embedding for email
 const embedding = await getEmbedding(emailDoc.body);
 // 2. query weaviate
 const res = await 
client.graphql.get().withClassName("Agenda").withNearVector(
{ vector: embedding, certainty: 0.65 }).withLimit(3).do();
 const contexts = res.data.Get.Agenda.map(a => 
a.text).join("\n---\n");
 // 3. call LLM
 const prompt = `You are a helpful sales assistant. Use these 
context 
docs:\n${contexts}\n\nEmail:\n${emailDoc.body}\n\nGenerate 
2 suggested replies: one short (<=40 words) one full reply (>=60 
words) with a clear CTA.`;
 const llmResp = await callLLM(prompt);
 // store returned suggestions in ES under email id
 await es.update({ index: "emails", id: emailDoc.messageId, doc: 
{ suggestedReplies: llmResp }});
}

Store product/agendas: create a Weaviate class Agenda with 
text property and push embeddings using weaviate client, or 
use the Weaviate REST API.

