14 — Implementation tips & gotchas
Gmail & OAuth2 — Gmail blocks plain username/password for 
many accounts; use XOAUTH2 or an app password for demo. 
For assignment use test IMAP accounts from any provider that 
allows username+password IMAP auth.
IMAP duplicate detection — dedupe by messageId (RFC 
Message-ID) or UID+mailbox to avoid reindexing.
Attachments — store attachments metadata in ES raw field or 
blob store (S3).
Rate limits & cost — if using OpenAI for every email, costs can 
grow; batch classification or use a lighter model / rule-based 
heuristics for low budget.
Security — secure credentials (do not commit .env), use TLS 
between services if exposing externally.
Elasticsearch memory — allocate enough memory; use 
ES_JAVA_OPTS e.g. -Xmx1g on dev machines with enough RAM.

